  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485 through the optional plug-in module, device as slave; address 1 to 247 (factory 1), broadcast is not supported. Baud rate 2400 to 38400, factory 9600; the manual gives 1 stop bit without parity as the factory setting.",
    "Measured values are 32-bit IEEE 754 floats in two registers, read with function 04 (input registers, the manual's 3X registers); settings are also two registers each, read with function 03 and written with function 16 (one parameter per message). A request is limited to 40 values (80 registers).",
    "Addresses are the protocol start addresses of the manual (register 30001 is address 0, 40001 is address 0), address base 0. Registers not listed are reserved by the manufacturer.",
    "The first register of each pair holds the most significant word by default; the manual lets this be changed with the register order parameter, so word order big is the factory default.",
    "Which values are valid depends on the network type: values marked with a cross in the manual for the system in use read as zero.",
    "Power factors are negative for inductive and positive for capacitive load. Energies are in k units (kWh, kvarh, kVAh, Ah) by default, or in M units (MWh, kAh for ampere-hours) when the energy prefix is set to M, so the unit written here is the default.",
    "The 'average over t' and 'maximum over t' values use the averaging time t; the averages are valid only after the first period.",
    "The manual does not state the data format of the settings other than saying every value is a 32-bit float, so they are given as float32.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
